# Security & secrets

Golden reference: `src/app/env.ts`, `src/middleware/requestLogger.ts`, `src/lib/observability/redact.ts`.

Complements `observability.mdc` (structured logging). This rule is the **hard prohibition** list.

## Purpose

AI debug logging often leaks production secrets. One `console.log(process.env)` or `logger.info({ headers: req.headers })` compromises the system.

## Required patterns

| Rule | Pattern |
| ---- | ------- |
| Env parsing | **Only** `src/app/env.ts` — `envSchema.parse(process.env)` |
| Config access | Import `env` from `env.ts` — never `process.env` in modules |
| Logging | `src/app/logger.ts` — never `console.log` in application code |
| HTTP logs | `requestLogger` — sensitive paths skip body logging |
| Alerts | `redactAlertPayload` before Discord/webhook outbound |
| Errors to clients | Generic message + `requestId` — no stack or env in JSON |

## Never log or return

- `process.env` or any env var value
- `Authorization` headers, cookies, session tokens, API keys
- Passwords, OTP codes, refresh tokens, presigned URLs with credentials
- Stripe webhook signing secrets, raw webhook bodies with PII
- Full `req.headers`, `req.cookies`, or `req.body` on auth/upload routes
- Database connection strings, `DATABASE_URL`, R2 secret keys

## Good examples

```ts
import { env } from "../../app/env.js";
import { logger } from "../../app/logger.js";

logger.error("payment_failed", {
  requestId: getRequestContext()?.requestId,
  userId,
  error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "unknown",
});
```

## Bad examples

```ts
console.log("config", process.env);
logger.debug("stripe", { key: env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY });
logger.info("login", { password: body.password, headers: req.headers });
res.status(500).json({ error: err.message, stack: err.stack, dbUrl: env.DATABASE_URL });
```

## Explicit prohibitions

- No `console.log` / `console.debug` in `src/` (tests excepted).
- No `process.env.*` outside `env.ts`.
- No logging full request/response objects on authenticated routes.
- No including secrets in `ConflictError` / `ValidationError` messages returned to clients.
- No committing `.env` or printing env in startup banners beyond “configured / not configured”.

## AI guidance

Debugging? Log IDs and operation names — not credentials. New env var? Schema in `env.ts` only. HTTP middleware or error handler changes? Re-check redaction paths. Response leakage: `response-contracts.mdc`.
